WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.000
Is it alive? One clue is never enough.

2
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.300
Living things grow, need water, air and food, react to changes, and make more of

3
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.680
their kind. A toy car moves, but it is not alive.

4
00:00:15.683 --> 00:00:18.823
Fill a basket with ten to twelve things from around the house.

5
00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:22.823
Mix a rock, a toy car, a dry leaf, an apple, and a houseplant.

6
00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:25.223
Add one or two large dry beans.

7
00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:30.547
Ask your child to sort everything into two piles, alive and not alive.

8
00:00:31.487 --> 00:00:33.707
Ask how they decided, and write down their rule.

9
00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:35.647
Do not correct it yet.

10
00:00:36.807 --> 00:00:40.067
Next, build a checklist from a pet or plant, and test each object.

11
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.440
Spend the most time on the seed, the toy car, and the dry leaf.

12
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.540
A resting seed is alive, though it shows few clues today, and a toy car is not.

13
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.020
It is fine to leave a question open.

14
00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.273
Stay with your child.

15
00:00:55.173 --> 00:00:58.713
Keep beans and other small objects away from children under four.

16
00:00:59.593 --> 00:01:01.353
Nothing from the basket is for eating.
